WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:11.025
GOES-18 is the third of the "GOES-R Series", the current generation of weather satellites operated by the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA).

00:11.594 --> 00:22.886
The current and next satellites of the Series will extend the availability of the Geostationary Operational Environmental Satellite (GOES) satellite system until 2037.

00:23.391 --> 00:27.396
The satellite is built by Lockheed Martin in Littleton, Colorado.

00:27.982 --> 00:35.039
It is based on the A2100A satellite bus and will have an expected useful life of 15 years.
